            <ArticleTitle>Use of intra-arterial papaverine for severe arterial spasm during radial cardiac catheterization.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>551-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary angiography and intervention can be performed safely using the radial artery. However, arterial spasm is often encountered and usually amenable to nitrate/verapamil therapy. Rarely, surgical intervention is required to remove catheters and wires. Intra-arterial papavarine can be used to treat severe radial artery spasm and prevent the need for urgent surgical intervention.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
